From 1211f00cd95d2ce1c71cc0150749425a97dc7e77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HelaFaye <dilsha21@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:30:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] esp32s3: I2C0/I2C1 masters

The S3 had no I2C controller. Both now run ESP-IDF's command lists
(COMD0-7: RSTART, WRITE with the address after a start, READ with the
final ACK level, STOP, END to pause and refill) over a QEMU I2C bus,
i2c0 or i2c1, with the 32-byte FIFOs, ACK checking (NACK ends the
transfer), SR counts and RESP_REC, the interrupts drivers wait for and
their timing at the configured SCL. The same block is in the C3/C6.

The S3 machine also selects AT24C EEPROMs.
